The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/envelope/envelope-06-gershgorin-vs-full-eigensystem.md`.

**Summary**: 5 findings (1 medium, 4 low). The key concern is that `from_continuous` rejects models based solely on Gershgorin bounds (conservative upper bound), which can cause false-positive rejections of stable multi-zone RC networks. The code already has full eigenvalue infrastructure (`eigenvalue_check`, `verify_stability`) but avoids it in the construction hot path due to nalgebra's Schur QR iteration concerns. Neither OCHRE nor EnergyPlus performs eigenvalue stability checks — both rely on physics-guaranteed stability from positive R/C parameters or Fourier-number-based heuristics.
